      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Silk Road primarily facilitated economic interconnectedness by acting as a global artery that enabled the long-distance exchange of luxury goods, raw materials, and currency across vast continents. It fostered the rise of specialized trade cities and clear economic hierarchies where wealthy merchants dictated market prices and controlled lucrative transit points. Furthermore, the constant flow of diverse commodities fueled a shared market economy that drove technological innovations, urban expansion, and sustained a continuous flow of wealth between East and West. These three pillars—commodity flow, urban economic hubs, and the resulting technological exchange—provide an excellent framework for structuring your lecture.",
